{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"group-phasea","type":"group","x":1620,"y":40,"width":2990,"height":380,"label":"Phase A: Modular Cleanup"},
		{"id":"group-phaseb","type":"group","x":4690,"y":40,"width":1030,"height":800,"label":"Phase B: Compiled Scheduler"},
		{"id":"group-phasec","type":"group","x":4690,"y":1020,"width":1030,"height":420,"label":"Phase C: Wire Thermal Reduction"},
		{"id":"group-guardr","type":"group","x":20,"y":40,"width":1520,"height":260,"label":"Guardrails"},
		{"id":"canvas-errors","type":"text","text":"## Errors\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-750,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"## Legend\n🔴 **Red** = To Do (ready)\n⬜ **Gray** = Blocked\n🟠 **Orange** = Doing\n🔵 **Cyan** = Ready to review\n🟢 **Green** = Done\n🟣 **Purple** = Proposed by agent","x":-540,"y":-310,"width":380,"height":230,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"canvas-warnings","type":"text","text":"## Warnings\n- XX-01 N/S-01 N/S-01 P3-03 Re-home Numba cache + AOT as startup-only work is outside all groups","x":-540,"y":-530,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"8f691f4e","type":"text","text":"## PAM-01 P1-01 Add __slots__ to EDMState\nAdd slots=True to EDMState dataclass in core/state.py. Eliminates __dict__ lookup overhead on ~50+ attribute accesses per step. Expected: 0.5-1.5 us/step.","x":1680,"y":80,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"1160ff9f","type":"text","text":"## PAM-02 P1-02 Scalar RNG in ignition\nReplace np_random.random(2) array alloc in ignition.py:581 with two scalar np_random.random() calls. Avoids per-step array allocation and float boxing. Expected: 0.5-1.0 us/step.","x":2170,"y":80,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"fca6958a","type":"text","text":"## PAM-03 P1-03 Remove redundant float() casts\nImplemented cast cleanup in ignition/wire; 1M-step fidelity PASS, measured plus 6.8 percent at 0.20 mm and plus 12.9 percent at 0.05 mm. Details: docs/realtime_optimization_execution_results.md.","x":2660,"y":80,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"8c990064","type":"text","text":"## PAM-04 P1-04 Non-Optional voltage/current\nChanged EDMState voltage/current defaults to 0.0 and removed hot-path None checks; 1M-step fidelity PASS, measured plus 0.7 percent at 0.20 mm and minus 0.1 percent at 0.05 mm. Details: docs/realtime_optimization_execution_results.md.","x":3150,"y":80,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b2a562df","type":"text","text":"## PBC-01 P2-01 Flat numeric hot-state bundle\nDefine pure-numeric state representation for ~30 scalars + 4 wire arrays. spark_status as 3 numeric scalars with NaN sentinel. No Python objects in hot path. EDMState remains public API.","x":4750,"y":80,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b9f45f24","type":"text","text":"## PBC-02 P2-02 Compiled @njit inner loop\nCompiled scheduler fixed for control-state sync and mode-dependent crater geometry. Validation: 112 pytest tests pass including 21 compiled-path tests. Reproducible bench_compiled.py shows real but smaller gains: about 1.40x at 0.20 mm and 1.30x at 0.05 mm on 200k repeated runs; 1M one-off A/B was about 1.20x and 1.17x. Fidelity is aligned within test/profile tolerances, not exact bitwise parity.","x":4750,"y":460,"width":420,"height":300,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"7e3b7897","type":"text","text":"## PBC-03 P2-03 Branch-consistent RNG architecture\nImplement multi-call RNG pattern: 2 draws always, conditional draws for ignition/location/crater. Preserves exact branch consumption pattern for fidelity. Co-developed with P2-02.","x":5240,"y":460,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"f0760043","type":"text","text":"## PBC-04 P2-04 Tighten step() fast path\nExtend existing ScalarAction/bypass machinery. Skip info dict + obs/reward on non-control steps. Return only (terminated, truncated) from inner path. Expected: 0.5-1.0 us/step.","x":5240,"y":80,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"812165b7","type":"text","text":"## PAM-06 P1-05r Slots on module param dataclasses\nExperiment evaluated and reverted: slots on module parameter dataclasses showed no steady-state gain and added rigidity. Findings: docs/realtime_optimization_non_wins.md.","x":3640,"y":80,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"4fced4b4","type":"text","text":"## GU-02 G-02 Fidelity lockstep check\nFor Phase 2 compiled path: run single-step comparison against modular reference path before the full 200k-step benchmark. Must match DEFAULT_FIDELITY_TOLERANCES (crater_count_abs=0, wire_temp_abs=0.5K, damage_abs=1e-4, position_abs=0.1um).","x":570,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"52cd1621","type":"text","text":"## GU-03 G-03 Dashboard refresh after each candidate\nUpdate performance_dashboard.html after each verified candidate. Ensures progress tracker stays current and sub-hotspot breakdown is visible for prioritizing the next cut.","x":1060,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"1d21b3c5","type":"text","text":"## GU-01 G-01 Same-session reprofile gate\nEvery candidate must be profiled in the same session as the previous candidate to eliminate thermal/frequency drift. Use scripts/profile_simulation.py with same-session A/B workflow.","x":80,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"20880e98","type":"text","text":"## XX-01 N/S-01 N/S-01 P3-03 Re-home Numba cache + AOT as startup-only work\nEnable cache=True and/or AOT compilation only as startup ergonomics. This does not improve steady-state realtime throughput, so it should not sit in the critical Phase C lane; replace or move PCW-03 into this non-critical group.","x":6910,"y":80,"width":280,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c16b0fb2","type":"text","text":"## PAM-07 P1-05 Drop convection-boundary idea for 1 us benchmark\nCurrent realtime contract uses servo_interval == dt == 1 us, so updating convection only at control boundaries is still every microstep and is not a meaningful optimization. Replace PAM-05 with PAM-06 or another measured Phase A win instead of pursuing this card.","x":4130,"y":80,"width":420,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"7cf2c66b","type":"text","text":"## PCW-01 P3-01 Active thermal window\nCompute full conduction-convection-damage only for segments near spark/contacts (+-5-10 segs). Cold tails updated every 100-500us. Reduces wire from O(N) to O(W) where W<<N. Expected: 7-50x wire reduction.","x":4750,"y":1060,"width":420,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"aa06438b","type":"text","text":"## PCW-02 P3-02 SIMD-friendly loop restructuring\nSplit interleaved thermal core into separate passes (dT_dt computation, temperature update, damage). Each becomes a clean vectorizable loop. Verify with numba --annotate-html. Expected: 0.1-0.5 us/step.","x":5240,"y":1060,"width":420,"height":240,"color":"6"}
	],
